# Commits on main since then that touch the same files:
# - ba75d85 agent-desktop: T0042: Resume a run: a run closed mid-way is kept and offered on the menu
#
# - e6b10dc agent-desktop: T0055: Working aura: the quiet ring under support towers when their aura works
#
# - 0f2cc36 agent-narcissus: T0019: Fast-forward: a 2x speed button for the wave phase
#
# - 1f3a65f Mattias S: Chokepoint: enemy hooks, effects and sounds outside the hub files
#   Most open tasks edit the same few hub files (EnemySystem 10, FxSystem 8,
#   Sfx 6), so with the file lock they could only be built one at a time.
#   New extension points, so a task adds its own file instead:
#
#   - systems/enemyHooks/: onKill, onLeak and a per-frame update, one file per
#     hook, listed in ENEMY_HOOKS (lock-free). Each is made once per run from
#     the run's systems, so its state starts fresh. The Splitter's split moved
#     there as the model (split.ts). EnemySystem only calls the hooks; its kill
#     block keeps every line the open designs anchor on, and leak hooks run
#     from update(), since one design replaces leak() wholesale.
#   - FxSystem: scene, track() and a new `full` check are public, so a new
#     effect is a function in systems/fx/<name>.ts.
#   - Sfx: tone() is public, and Sfx.ts is lock-free: tasks only add sound
#     methods there, which merge.ts joins without an agent.
#
#   CLAUDE.md, ARCHITECTURE.md and the architect prompt teach the new
#   recipes. The existing designs still apply as written.

